_getitem_lowerdim.\n1018 |         \"\"\"\n1019 |         retval = self.obj\n1020 |         # Selecting columns before rows is significantly faster\n1021 |         start_val = (self.ndim - len(tup)) + 1\n1022 |         for i, key in enumerate(reversed(tup)):\n1023 |             i = self.ndim - i - start_val\n1024 |             if com.is_null_slice(key):\n1025 |                 continue\n1026 | \n1027 |             retval = getattr(retval, self.name)._getitem_axis(key, axis=i)\n1028 |             # We should never have retval.ndim < self.ndim, as that should\n1029 |             #  be handled by the _getitem_lowerdim call above.\n1030 |             assert retval.ndim == self.ndim\n1031 | \n1032 |         if retval is self.obj:\n1033 |             # if all axes were a null slice (`df.loc[:, :]`), ensure we still\n1034 |             # return a new object (https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/pull/49469)\n1035 |             retval = retval.copy(deep=False)\n1036 | \n1037 |         return retval\n```\n"}, {"content": "Based on the analysis of the issue and the code, I can now provide the locations that need modification to implement the requested feature improvement. The issue requests increasing verbosity in error messages when a string accessor error occurs, particularly by including the inferred data type.\n\nHere are the relevant locations:\n\n```\npandas/core/strings/accessor.py\nline: 257-258\nfunction: StringMethods._validate\ndescription: This is where the AttributeError is currently raised without inferred_dtype\n\npandas/core/dtypes/common.py\nline: 1776\nfunction: is_dtype_equal\ndescription: Contains type checking logic used for determining dtype equality\n\npandas/core/construction.py\nline: 425-487\nfunction: extract_array\ndescription: Used to extract array data for type inference\n\npandas/core/dtypes/cast.py\nline: 1028-1037\nfunction: convert_dtypes\ndescription: Contains dtype inference logic\n\npandas/core/arrays/string_.py\ndescription: Contains Strin