       x : float or array-like\n2341 |             The x coordinates of the bars. See also *align* for the\n2342 |             alignment of the bars to the coordinates.\n2343 | \n2344 |         height : float or array-like\n2345 |             The height(s) of the bars.\n2346 | \n2347 |             Note that if *bottom* has units (e.g. datetime), *height* should be in\n2348 |             units that are a difference from the value of *bottom* (e.g. timedelta).\n2349 | \n2350 |         width : float or array-like, default: 0.8\n2351 |             The width(s) of the bars.\n2352 | \n2353 |             Note that if *x* has units (e.g. datetime), then *width* should be in\n2354 |             units that are a difference (e.g. timedelta) around the *x* values.\n2355 | \n2356 |         bottom : float or array-like, default: 0\n2357 |             The y coordinate(s) of the bottom side(s) of the bars.\n2358 | \n2359 |             Note that if *bottom* has units, then the y-axis will get a Locator and\n2360 |             Formatter appropriate for the units (e.g. dates, or categorical).\n2361 | \n2362 |         align : {'center', 'edge'}, default: 'center'\n2363 |             Alignment of the bars to the *x* coordinates:\n2364 | \n2365 |             - 'center': Center the base on the *x* positions.\n2366 |             - 'edge': Align the left edges of the bars with the *x* positions.\n2367 | \n2368 |             To align the bars on the right edge pass a negative *width* and\n2369 |             ``align='edge'``.\n2370 | \n2371 |         Returns\n2372 |         -------\n2373 |         `.BarContainer`\n2374 |             Container with all the bars and optionally errorbars.\n2375 | \n2376 |         Other Parameters\n2377 |         ----------------\n2378 |         color : :mpltype:`color` or list of :mpltype:`color`, optional\n2379 |             The colors of the bar faces.\n2380 | \n2381 |         edgecolor : :mpltype:`color` or list of :mpltype:`color`, optional\n2382 |             The colors of the bar edges.\n2383 | \n2384 |         linewidth : float or array-like, optional\n2385 |             Width of the bar edge(s). If 0, don't draw edges.\n2386 | \n2387 |         tick_label : str or list of str, optional\n2388 |             The tick labels of the bars.\n2389 |             Default: None (Use default numeric labels.)\n2390 | \n2391 |         label : str or list of str, optional\n2392 |             A single label is attached to the resulting `.BarContainer` as a\n2393 |             label for the whole dataset.\n2394 |             If a list is provided, it must be the same length as *x* and\n2395 |             labels the individual bars. Repeated labels are not de-duplicated\n2396 |             and will cause repeated label entries, so this is best used when\n2397 |             bars also differ in style (e.g., by passing a list to *color*.)\n2398 | \n2399 |         xerr, yerr : float or array-like of shape(N,) or shape(2, N), optional\n2400 |             If not *None*, add horizontal / vertical errorbars to the bar tips.\n2401 |             The values are +/- sizes relative to the data:\n2402 | \n2403 |             - scalar: symmetric +/- values for all bars\n2404 |             - shape(N,): symmetric +/- values for each bar\n2405 |             - shape(2, N): Separate - and + values for each bar. First row\n2406 |               contains the lower errors, the second row contains the upper\n2407 |               errors.\n2408 |             - *None*: No errorbar. (Default)\n2409 | \n2410 |             See :doc:`/gallery/statistics/errorbar_features` for an example on\n2411 |             the usage of *xerr* and *yerr*.\n2412 | \n2413 |         ecolor : :mpltype:`color` or list of :mpltype:`color`, default: 'black'\n2414 |             The line color of the errorbars.\n2415 | \n2416 |         capsize : float, default: :rc:`errorbar.capsize`\n2417 |            The length of the error bar caps in points.\n2418 | \n2419 |         error_kw : dict, optional\n2420 |             Dictionary of keyword arguments to be passed to the\n2421 |             `~.Axes.errorbar` method. Values of *ecolor* or *capsize* defined\n2422 |             here take precedence over the independent keyword arguments.\n2423 | \n2424 |         log : bool, default: False\n2425 |             If *True*, set the y-axis to be log scale.\n2426 | \n2427 |         data : indexable object, optional\n2428 |             DATA_PARAMETER_PLACEHOLDER\n2429 | \n2430 |         **kwargs : `.Rectangle` properties\n2431 | \n2432 |         %(Rectangle:kwdoc)s\n2433 | \n2434 |         See Also\n2435 |         --------\n2436 |         barh : Plot a horizontal bar plot.\n2437 | \n2438 |         Notes\n2439 |         -----\n2440 |         Stacked bars can be achieved by passing individual *bottom* values per\n2441 |         bar. See :doc:`/gallery/lines_bars_and_markers/bar_stacked`.\n2442 |         \"\"\"\n2443 |         kwargs = cbook.normalize_kwargs(kwargs, mpatches.Patch)\n2444 |         color = kwargs.pop('color', None)\n2445 |         if color is None:\n2446 |             color = self._get_patches_for_fill.get_next_color()\n2447 |         edgecolor = kwargs.pop('edgecolor', None)\n2448 |         linewidth = kwargs.pop('linewidth', None)\n2449 |         hatch = kwargs.pop('hatch', None)\n2450 | \n2451 |         # Because xerr and yerr will be passed to errorbar, most dimension\n2452 |         # checking and processing will be left to the errorbar method.\n2453 |         xerr = kwargs.pop('xerr', None)\n2454 |         yerr = kwargs.pop('yerr', None)\n2455 |         error_kw = kwargs.pop('error_kw', None)\n2456 |         error_kw = {} if error_kw is None else error_kw.copy()\n2457 |         ezorder = error_kw.pop('zorder', None)\n2458 |         if ezorder is None:\n2459 |             ezorder = kwargs.get('zorder', None)\n2460 |             if ezorder is not None:\n2461 |                 # If using the bar zorder, increment slightly to make sure\n2462 |        