    updatex = True\n1262 |             updatey = True\n1263 |             if self.name == \"rectilinear\":\n1264 |                 datalim = lines.get_datalim(self.transData)\n1265 |                 t = lines.get_transform()\n1266 |                 updatex, updatey = t.contains_branch_seperately(self.transData)\n1267 |                 minx = np.nanmin(datalim.xmin)\n1268 |                 maxx = np.nanmax(datalim.xmax)\n1269 |                 miny = np.nanmin(datalim.ymin)\n1270 |                 maxy = np.nanmax(datalim.ymax)\n1271 |             else:\n1272 |                 minx = np.nanmin(masked_verts[..., 0])\n1273 |                 maxx = np.nanmax(masked_verts[..., 0])\n1274 |                 miny = np.nanmin(masked_verts[..., 1])\n1275 |                 maxy = np.nanmax(masked_verts[..., 1])\n1276 | \n1277 |             corners = (minx, miny), (maxx, maxy)\n1278 |             self.update_datalim(corners, updatex, updatey)\n1279 |             self._request_autoscale_view()\n1280 |         return lines\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"matplotlib/axes/_axes.py:vlines\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `lib/matplotlib/axes/_axes.py:Axes.violin`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n8570 | def violin(self, vpstats, positions=None, vert=None,\n8571 |                orientation='vertical', widths=0.5, showmeans=False,\n8572 |                showextrema=True, showmedians=False, side='both'):\n8573 |         \"\"\"\n8574 |         Draw a violin plot from pre-computed statistics.\n8575 | \n8576 |         Draw a violin plot for each column of *vpstats*. Each filled area\n8577 |         extends to represent the entire data range, with optional lines at the\n8578 |         mean, the median, the minimum, the maximum, and the quantiles values.\n8579 | \n8580 |         Parameters\n8581 |         ----------\n8582 |         vpstats : list of dicts\n8583 |             A list of dictionaries containing stats for each violin plot.\n8584 |             Required keys are:\n8585 | \n8586 |             - ``coords``: A list of scalars containing the coordinates that\n8587 |               the violin's kernel density estimate were evaluated at.\n8588 | \n8589 |             - ``vals``: A list of scalars containing the values of the\n8590 |               kernel density estimate at each of the coordinates given\n8591 |               in *coords*.\n8592 | \n8593 |             - ``mean``: The mean value for this violin's dataset.\n8594 | \n8595 |             - ``median``: The median value for this violin's dataset.\n8596 | \n8597 |             - ``min``: The minimum value for this violin's dataset.\n8598 | \n8599 |             - ``max``: The maximum value for this violin's dataset.\n8600 | \n8601 |             Optional keys are:\n8602 | \n8603 |             - ``quantiles``: A list of scalars containing the quantile values\n8604 |               for this violin's dataset.\n8605 | \n8606 |         positions : array-like, default: [1, 2, ..., n]\n8607 |             The positions of the violins; i.e. coordinates on the x-axis for\n8608 |             vertical violins (or y-axis for horizontal violins).\n8609 | \n8610 |         vert : bool, optional\n8611 |             .. deprecated:: 3.10\n8612 |                 Use *orientation* instead.\n8613 | \n8614 |                 If this is given during the deprecation period, it overrides\n8615 |                 the *orientation* parameter.\n8616 | \n8617 |             If True, plots the violins vertically.\n8618 |             If False, plots the violins horizontally.\n8619 | \n8620 |         orientation : {'vertical', 'horizontal'}, default: 'vertical'\n8621 |             If 'horizontal', plots the violins horizontally.\n8622 |             Otherwise, plots the violins vertically.\n8623 | \n8624 |             .. versionadded:: 3.10\n8625 | \n8626 |         widths : float or array-like, default: 0.5\n8627 |             The maximum width of each violin in units of the *positions* a